+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: cli-sum-stdin
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, cli, durations]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 1
+lane: light
+tier: 1
+summary: "timeparse CLI: --sum total, '-' stdin inputs, report all invalid durations"
+---
+
+# SPEC: cli-sum-stdin
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`timeparse.cli.main` stops at the first bad duration and only accepts argv. Users piping lists of durations need stdin input, a total, and a complete error report in one run.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+- `--sum` prints a single total-seconds line.
+- `-` reads durations from stdin, in order, mixed freely with argv.
+- One run reports every invalid input; stdout stays empty and exit code is 2 when any is invalid.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: sum of arguments
+**Given** argv `["--sum", "1h", "30m"]`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is exactly `5400\n` and the return value is 0
+
+### S2: stdin mixed with sum
+**Given** stdin `"1m\n\n2m\n"` and argv `["-", "--sum"]`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is exactly `180\n` (blank line ignored) and the return value is 0
+**And** with argv `["30s", "-"]` and no `--sum`, stdout is `30\n60\n120\n` (order kept)
+
+### S3: every invalid input reported
+**Given** argv `["1h", "x", "2q"]`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stderr is exactly `error: invalid duration: 'x'\nerror: invalid duration: '2q'\n`, stdout is empty, and the return value is 2
+**And** an invalid stdin line `"  zz  "` is reported as `'zz'` (stripped text), also with `--sum`
+
+### S4: default output unchanged
+**Given** argv `["1h", "30m"]` without `--sum`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is `3600\n1800\n` and the return value is 0
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Changes to `parse_duration` grammar or `timeparse/format.py`.
+- New flags beyond `--sum`; output formats other than integer seconds.
+- Streaming/lazy stdin processing.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | already used in `tests/` and `pyproject.toml` |
+| Compatibility | `main(argv: list[str] | None) -> int` signature unchanged | existing callers/tests |
+| Dependencies | stdlib only | none exist today |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none — additive flag and an error-reporting change on a pre-1.0 CLI; trivially revertable.
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 / AC-001 | unit | `test_sum_of_arguments` |
+| S2 / AC-002 | unit | `test_stdin_mixed_with_sum`, `test_stdin_keeps_order` |
+| S3 / AC-003 | unit | `test_all_invalid_reported` |
+| S4 / AC-004 | unit | `test_default_output_unchanged` |
+| AC-005 | unit (property) | `test_sum_equals_sum_of_lines` |
+
+### AC-001: Sum of arguments
+`--sum` prints only the total seconds, one line (S1). Oracle: golden `5400` = 3600+1800 by hand arithmetic.
+
+### AC-002: Stdin input
+`-` reads stripped, non-blank stdin lines, in position among args (S2). Oracle: golden `180` from spec example.
+
+### AC-003: All invalid inputs reported
+All invalid inputs (argv and stdin) listed on stderr, stdout empty, return 2 (S3). Oracle: golden stderr text from the ask.
+
+### AC-004: Default output unchanged
+Without `--sum`, one seconds line per duration (S4). Oracle: golden from existing behavior.
+
+### AC-005: Sum equals sum of per-line outputs
+For any valid inputs, `--sum` output equals the sum of the lines printed without `--sum`. Oracle: property, holds regardless of implementation.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Lane `light`: one source file plus tests, one session, no irreversible decision. Not skipped by Step 0: CLI behavior/contract changes.
+- Interview: single round, ask fully specified; no question tool used (autopilot `auto_full`). Defaults chosen: `-` given twice reads stdin once (second read is empty); empty total with `--sum` prints `0`; stdin with no lines and no `--sum` prints nothing, returns 0; a whitespace-only argv item is invalid (`''`); at least one argument still required by argparse.
+- Spec validator not dispatched: light lane, `irreversible_decisions: []`.
